Adapted pi material (MIT):

- `packages/harness/src/compaction.ts` — context-compaction algorithm
  (cut-point selection, transcript serialization, incremental summary chaining).
  The `SUMMARIZATION_PROMPT` and `UPDATE_SUMMARIZATION_PROMPT` prompt strings
  are verbatim copies of pi's summarization prompts.
- `packages/harness/src/provider.ts` — the retry / error-classification registry
  is ported from pi-ai's `utils/{retry,provider-retry,overflow}.ts`.
- `packages/harness/src/workspace.ts` — `normalizeForFuzzyMatch` and the
  robust-edit matching strategy are ported from pi's `edit-diff.ts`.
- `packages/harness/src/output.ts` — bounded output windows + ANSI sanitizing;
  informed by pi's `chord/src/output.ts`, reimplemented (not copied).

Design conventions adopted from other MIT projects (reimplemented, not copied):

- kimi-code (https://github.com/MoonshotAI/kimi-code, MIT, (c) 2026 Moonshot AI):
  `<skill-loaded>` delivery convention, plugin command model.
- deepseek-harness (https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness, MIT,
  (c) 2026 DeepSeek): NDJSON run-stream projection shape and field/line bounds.
- opencode (https://github.com/sst/opencode, MIT, (c) 2025 opencode):
  flat command catalogue, plugin hooks and `{ path, options }` entry form.

No source code is copied from these three; only ideas and wire shapes, each with
an attribution comment at the point of use in `packages/harness/src/`.
